Vasiṣṭha names father, mother, teacher as three gurus --- Vasiṣṭha bids Rāma obey assembly, mother, begging Bharata --- Rāma says parents gifts cannot be repaid --- Rāma vows father command shall never prove false --- Bharata spreads kuśa and vows fasting before hut --- Rāma forbids royal fasting and bids rise for Ayōdhyā --- Citizens call Rāma right and beyond turning --- Bharata sips water, disavows kingdom, offers fourteen forest years --- Rāma bars substitutes, justifies Kaikēyī, frees father from falsehood --- Rāma trusts Bharata and vows return to rule together
